  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Seasonable Warmup through Veterans Day \n\nMostly sunny, breezy and warmer today with max temps in the mid\n50s to upper 60s or +8-15 degrees higher than Monday. Max wind \ngusts 20-30 mph from the west. Low humidity and breezy conditions\ncould result in an elevated risk of wildfire spread across \nsouth central PA this afternoon (Lower Ridge/Valley and \nSoutheast districts). Pleasant and seasonably warm conditions \ncontinue for Veterans Day with highs +5-10 degrees above the \nhistorical average and more clouds than sun.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2: Late week rain and potential high elevation\nsnow accumulation\n\nLow pressure tracking through the Ohio Valley will bring\nperiods of rain to CPA late Wednesday night into Thursday. \nRainfall amounts are in the 0.10-0.50\" range ending 00Z Friday. \nFcst highs Thursday in the mid 40s/50s are 10 degrees lower than\nWednesday.\n\nA cold air injection associated with an intensifying upper\ntrough over the Eastern U.S. should allow for rain and higher\nelevation snow Thursday night into Friday. Areas most likely to\nsee the first snow accumulation of the season are in the \nEndless Mtns/Poconos, Northern Tier, NW Alleghenies, and Laurel\nHighlands (generally north & west of I-99/I-80). The pattern \neventually transitions to a lake effect/upslope precip event \nover the weekend with additional snow accumulation possible.  \n\nKEY MESSAGE 3: Windy and colder Friday through the weekend\n\nGusty winds and below average temperatures will make for a\nrather chilly stretch from Friday through the weekend. Highs in\nthe 35-50F range with a wind chill factor. For context, its been\nabout 200 days since it was this cold during the day.",
